From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garvit Surana <251430630+garvitsurana271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:55:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nouveau): bound a busy fence wait by the clock and look
 whether its GPU still answers each 10 ms of it, where a channel idle on a GPU
 off the bus spun until the step watchdog stopped it, as neither its 15 s
 timeout nor its once-a-tick look ever came due on jiffies that did not move

nouveau_fence_wait_busy() never blocks, and on Stela's Linux layer
jiffies move only when a task resumes or a service pass runs, so its
jiffies timeout and patch 0218's "once a tick" nvkm_device_gone() look
never fired inside one step. At a stop after an RTX 3050 Mobile left
the bus, nouveau_drm_shutdown() idled each channel through this wait
and the step watchdog ended it after 30 s, losing the end of the boot
log. The wait now also ends once what was left of the fence's timeout
has passed by ktime_get(), and looks at the device at once and then
each NOUVEAU_FENCE_GONE_MS of that clock, as r535_gsp_gone() does.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
index 8603e91673361837213d2cb9ca3fb1f27b0a0e2c..4a2bedd8da82e8232df2bd6729665e75aa41fdc3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
@@ -310,15 +310,33 @@ nouveau_fence_device(struct nouveau_fence *fence)
 	return device;
 }
 
+/*
+ * How often, by the clock, a busy wait for a fence looks whether its GPU
+ * still answers MMIO (nvkm_device_gone()).
+ */
+#define NOUVEAU_FENCE_GONE_MS 10
+
 static int
 nouveau_fence_wait_busy(struct nouveau_fence *fence, bool intr)
 {
-	unsigned long looked = jiffies;
+	/*
+	 * The spin is bounded by ktime as well as by jiffies, and looks at the
+	 * device by ktime: a host whose jiffies do not move while a task spins
+	 * without blocking (Stela's Linux layer moves them when a task resumes
+	 * or reads the clock) would otherwise never see the fence's timeout
+	 * pass nor a look come due. The ktime bound is what is left of the
+	 * fence's timeout now.
+	 */
+	long left = (long)(fence->timeout - jiffies);
+	ktime_t start = ktime_get();
+	s64 limit = left > 0 ? jiffies_to_msecs(left) : 0;
+	s64 looked = -NOUVEAU_FENCE_GONE_MS, waited;
 	struct nvkm_device *device;
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	while (!nouveau_fence_done(fence)) {
-		if (time_after_eq(jiffies, fence->timeout)) {
+		waited = ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), start);
+		if (time_after_eq(jiffies, fence->timeout) || waited >= limit) {
 			ret = -EBUSY;
 			break;
 		}
@@ -326,10 +344,10 @@ nouveau_fence_wait_busy(struct nouveau_fence *fence, bool intr)
 		/*
 		 * A GPU off the bus signals nothing: the spin would last its whole
 		 * 15 s for each fence, and a channel teardown idles every channel
-		 * of a file in turn. Look once a tick.
+		 * of a file in turn. Look at once, then each NOUVEAU_FENCE_GONE_MS.
 		 */
-		if (jiffies != looked) {
-			looked = jiffies;
+		if (waited >= looked + NOUVEAU_FENCE_GONE_MS) {
+			looked = waited;
 			device = nouveau_fence_device(fence);
 			if (device && nvkm_device_gone(device)) {
 				ret = -ENODEV;
